## @PixelatedManThe2nd — Issue

This is my first time using this site ,so I apologize for any inconvenience. Also my english is slightly crooked, so I'll try explaining as good as I can. 

Ever since I've moved from pro c to ark 5 I've had a problem with the overclock setting on my psp 03g ( the 3006 more specifically).

Before installing ark 5 I made sure to format my SD entirely and also revert my firmware back to it's original using chronoswitch. 

After that I went ahead and installed ark 5 and it went great.

But there's a problem with the overclock setting; for example, every time I set the game clock over 333mhz (383 and above) and try launching a game ,the psp logo briefly appears only to be followed by a black screen for a couple of seconds after which it completely shuts down and restarts. This also goes for the custom launcher, it just refuses to load. instead it crashes. completely.

This goes for the xmb as well. If I try to set the clock above 333mhz (383 and above) it simply goes to a black screen for some seconds only to crash and restart the console 

I did actually use the experimental overclock tester that came with the fasterark folder,  and I can confirm that the console can go as far as 468mhz so I really don't understand why this happens.

Also I don't have any plugins that could interfere with anything (cxmb being the only one active).

...Although I did manage to find a "temporary fix":

After using the experimental overclock tester, im able to  set the game clock AS WELL as the xmb clock to whatever frequency I previously couldn't use, and the games will run normally, but only for the current session! Once I turn off the console and turn it back on I have no choice but to use the experimental overclock tester AGAIN in order to overclock the console once more. And I have to do this EVERYTIME I turn on the psp.

I'm not entirely sure if I messed up something during the installation or if this is intentional,  but I hope that maybe there's a fix for this (or an explanation at the very least).

Cheers.

